{
  "key": "mitsubishi-ecodan-a1m",
  "label": "Mitsubishi Ecodan (MelcoBEMS MINI A1M)",
  "source": "Loxone Library template Mitshubishi Heat Pump (mitshubishi-heat-pump-1197 v1.0.0) + Procon A1M ATW Modbus register tables v1.0.7",
  "values": "loxone",
  "notes": [
    "Names as in the Loxone Library template, so they match the objects in Loxone. Registers marked extra are in the A1M but not in that template: add them as a Modbus sensor in Loxone to use them.",
    "Force DHW (37) starts one tap-water cycle up to the tank setpoint; the unit puts it back to 0 itself.",
    "Holiday (38) is writable on the A1M but only a sensor in the Library template; DHW / heating prohibit (39, 40, 42) are read only on firmware 3.0.28+.",
    "Tap-water setpoint above ~55 °C: the booster or immersion heater helps. Keep hpMaxC at what the heat pump reaches on its own.",
    "Tank Water Temp Target accepts up to 70 °C; LoxSuite only goes above the buffer maximum for the legionella cycle."
  ],
